"## Task 1: Dataset Initialization\n",
"In this section, we initialize the core sales data for Wanjiku's Gikomba clothing stall using native Python data structures (dictionaries and lists) without external library dependencies."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"# Dataset provided for Wanjiku's Gikomba Stall\n",
"daily_sales = [\n",
"    {"day": "Mon", "dresses": 12, "tshirts": 25, "jeans": 8},\n",
"    {"day": "Tue", "dresses": 15, "tshirts": 18, "jeans": 10},\n",
"    {"day": "Wed", "dresses": 8,  "tshirts": 30, "jeans": 5},\n",
"    {"day": "Thu", "dresses": 20, "tshirts": 22, "jeans": 15},\n",
"    {"day": "Fri", "dresses": 25, "tshirts": 40, "jeans": 20},\n",
"    {"day": "Sat", "dresses": 35, "tshirts": 50, "jeans": 30},\n",
"    {"day": "Sun", "dresses": 10, "tshirts": 15, "jeans": 5}\n",
"]\n",
"\n",
"prices = {"dresses": 1200, "tshirts": 500, "jeans": 1800}\n",
"costs = {"dresses": 700, "tshirts": 250, "jeans": 1000}\n",
"inventory = {"dresses": 15, "tshirts": 30, "jeans": 10}"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Task 2: Calculate Weekly Totals & Financial Metrics\n",
"We define the week_totals() function to compute total units sold per item category, total weekly revenue, total cost of goods sold (COGS), and overall profit."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"def week_totals(sales_data, item_prices, item_costs):\n",
"    """\n",
"    Calculates weekly sales units, revenue, costs, and profit for all items.\n",
"    \n",
"    Parameters:\n",
"        sales_data (list): List of daily sales dictionaries.\n",
"        item_prices (dict): Unit selling prices per item category.\n",
"        item_costs (dict): Unit wholesale cost per item category.\n",
"        \n",
"    Returns:\n",
"        dict: Comprehensive summary of weekly sales metrics.\n",
"    """\n",
"    totals = {"dresses": 0, "tshirts": 0, "jeans": 0}\n",
"    total_revenue = 0\n",
"    total_cost = 0\n",
"    \n",
"    for record in sales_data:\n",
"        for item in totals:\n",
"            units = record[item]\n",
"            totals[item] += units\n",
"            total_revenue += units * item_prices[item]\n",
"            total_cost += units * item_costs[item]\n",
"            \n",
"    total_profit = total_revenue - total_cost\n",
"    \n",
"    return {\n",
"        "units_sold": totals,\n",
"        "total_revenue": total_revenue,\n",
"        "total_cost": total_cost,\n",
"        "total_profit": total_profit\n",
"    }\n",
"\n",
"# Compute weekly financial metrics\n",
"weekly_summary = week_totals(daily_sales, prices, costs)\n",
"print("Weekly Units Sold:", weekly_summary["units_sold"])\n",
"print(f"Total Revenue: KES {weekly_summary['total_revenue']:,}")\n",
"print(f"Total Profit:  KES {weekly_summary['total_profit']:,}")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Task 3: Day Performance Classification\n",
"We implement the classify_day() function to categorize daily performance based on total revenue generated."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"def classify_day(daily_revenue):\n",
"    """\n",
"    Classifies a daily revenue amount into performance tiers.\n",
"    \n",
"    Parameters:\n",
"        daily_revenue (float/int): Total revenue generated in a single day.\n",
"        \n",
"    Returns:\n",
"        str: 'High' if revenue > 50,000 KES, 'Average' if between 30,000 and 50,000 KES, else 'Low'.\n",
"    """\n",
"    if daily_revenue > 50000:\n",
"        return "High"\n",
"    elif daily_revenue >= 30000:\n",
"        return "Average"\n",
"    else:\n",
"        return "Low"\n",
"\n",
"# Classify each day in the sales record\n",
"daily_classifications = []\n",
"for record in daily_sales:\n",
"    day_rev = (record["dresses"] * prices["dresses"]) + \\n",
"              (record["tshirts"] * prices["tshirts"]) + \\n",
"              (record["jeans"] * prices["jeans"])\n",
"    daily_classifications.append({\n",
"        "day": record["day"],\n",
"        "revenue": day_rev,\n",
"        "tier": classify_day(day_rev)\n",
"    })\n",
"\n",
"for day_info in daily_classifications:\n",
"    print(f"{day_info['day']}: KES {day_info['revenue']:,} -> {day_info['tier']}")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Task 4: Best and Worst Performing Days\n",
"We identify the days with the highest and lowest overall revenue using iterative comparisons."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"best_day = max(daily_classifications, key=lambda x: x["revenue"])\n",
"worst_day = min(daily_classifications, key=lambda x: x["revenue"])\n",
"\n",
"print(f"Best Day:  {best_day['day']} with KES {best_day['revenue']:,}")\n",
"print(f"Worst Day: {worst_day['day']} with KES {worst_day['revenue']:,}")"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Task 5: Inventory Reorder Strategy\n",
"We design the check_reorder_needs() function to evaluate remaining inventory against average daily demand to determine stock replenishment requirements."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"def check_reorder_needs(current_inv, units_sold, threshold_days=2):\n",
"    """\n",
"    Determines which items require inventory reordering based on remaining days of stock.\n",
"    \n",
"    Parameters:\n",
"        current_inv (dict): Current remaining stock counts per item.\n",
"        units_sold (dict): Total units sold over 7 days.\n",
"        threshold_days (int): Minimum acceptable days of stock remaining before reordering.\n",
"        \n",
"    Returns:\n",
"        dict: Reorder recommendations detailing status and recommended restock quantity.\n",
"    """\n",
"    reorder_summary = {}\n",
"    for item, stock in current_inv.items():\n",
"        avg_daily_sales = units_sold[item] / 7.0\n",
"        days_remaining = stock / avg_daily_sales if avg_daily_sales > 0 else 999\n",
"        \n",
"        needs_reorder = days_remaining < threshold_days\n",
"        # Target 7 days of buffer stock on reorder\n",
"        recommended_qty = max(0, int((avg_daily_sales * 7) - stock)) if needs_reorder else 0\n",
"        \n",
"        reorder_summary[item] = {\n",
"            "current_stock": stock,\n",
"            "avg_daily_sales": round(avg_daily_sales, 2),\n",
"            "days_remaining": round(days_remaining, 1),\n",
"            "reorder_needed": needs_reorder,\n",
"            "recommended_order_qty": recommended_qty\n",
"        }\n",
"    return reorder_summary\n",
"\n",
"reorder_status = check_reorder_needs(inventory, weekly_summary["units_sold"])\n",
"for item, details in reorder_status.items():\n",
"    print(f"{item.title()}: Stock={details['current_stock']} | Days Left={details['days_remaining']} | Reorder={details['reorder_needed']}")"
]
},
