"## Recommendations for Wanjiku\n",
"\n",
"Based on the analysis of weekly sales, profitability margins, and current stock levels, here are three actionable, data-backed recommendations for Wanjiku:\n",
"\n",
"1. Capitalize on Weekend Peak Traffic (Friday & Saturday):\n",
"   - Finding: Saturday generated the highest revenue (KES 114,000), followed by Friday (KES 86,000), accounting for over 52% of total weekly revenue.\n",
"   - Action: Ensure maximum stall staffing on Fridays and Saturdays. Offer bundled deals (e.g., buying a dress and t-shirt together) during these peak days to maximize customer basket size.\n",
"\n",
"2. Prioritize T-Shirt Inventory & High Margin Products:\n",
"   - Finding: T-Shirts are the highest volume item sold (198 units), but Jeans deliver the highest unit profit margin (KES 800 per pair vs KES 250 per T-Shirt).\n",
"   - Action: Reorder T-Shirts immediately as current stock (30 units) will run out in less than 1.1 days. Use profits generated from high-margin Jeans sales to fund larger wholesale orders of T-Shirts to prevent stockouts.\n",
"\n",
"3. Address Low Mid-Week & Sunday Performance (Wed & Sun):\n",
"   - Finding: Sunday (KES 28,500) and Wednesday (KES 33,600) recorded the lowest sales performance of the week.\n",
"   - Action: Use Wednesdays for restocking and inventory audit. Run targeted clearance discounts or promotional sales on Sundays to clear slow-moving inventory and convert quiet days into steady cash flow."
]
